WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit
2: Celebrations and Festivals.

2
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.540
Welcome to Unit 2!

3
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.920
In this unit you will explore celebrations
and festivals from around the world,

4
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:18.160
with a special focus on traditions that matter to
communities across East Africa and the Muslim world.

5
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.520
Festivals bring people together.

6
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:26.260
They remind us of our history, our values,
and the things that make each culture unique.

7
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:33.560
Whether it is the joy of Eid al-Fitr after a month of
fasting, the colourful lanterns of a harvest celebration,

8
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:38.740
or the excitement of a local sports
day, every festival has a story to tell.

9
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:44.920
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:51.620
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
understand texts about different festivals and celebrations.

11
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:58.400
you will also use prepositions of time (in,
on, at) correctly in speech and writing.

12
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:04.070
you will also recognise and form compound
adjectives (hand-made, brightly-coloured).

13
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:06.640
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:15.520
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: benevolent,
charismatic, determined, diligent, enthusiastic, industrious.

15
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:21.080
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:24.980
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:35.300
The reading sequence includes Celebrations and Festivals:
source text 1 and Celebrations and Festivals: source text 2.

18
00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:36.880
Read actively.

19
00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:41.680
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:45.460
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.600
The first language focus is How to Use Them: Step by Step.

22
00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:58.460
Step 1 — Use IN for longer periods of time: Think of
in as a big container that holds a stretch of time.

23
00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:04.740
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.360
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Compare Two Festivals.

25
00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:14.100
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.700
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.100
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:22.660
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:28.640
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:30.920
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.660
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
